+// True when aggressive checkerboarding (WEBKIT_CHECKERBOARD_DURING_SCROLL) is
+// enabled. See CoordinatedBackingStoreProxy: during a fast fling the backing store
+// deliberately leaves the newly-exposed viewport region untiled so it "shows the
+// page background". But CoordinatedBackingStore::paintToTextureMapper only paints
+// the tiles that exist -- nothing fills the gap. The page background is put there
+// solely by the clear() below, which for an opaque page upstream restricts to
+// AsyncScrolling composites. The checkerboard hold, however, also recomposites via
+// RenderingUpdate (m_pendingTileCreation -> isWaitingForTiles -> the settle tail),
+// and on those frames the opaque-background clear was skipped -- so the recycled
+// swap-chain target showed stale prior-frame content in the gap, i.e. the "glitch"
+// instead of a clean background. When checkerboarding is on we therefore clear the
+// opaque background on every composite too. The clear is scissored to the current
+// repaint/damage region (TextureMapper keeps GL_SCISSOR_TEST enabled and the clip
+// stack constrains the box), so it never erases undamaged tiles; the only cost is a
+// fullscreen clear while actively scrolling, which already happened via AsyncScrolling.
+static bool checkerboardClearsOpaqueBackground()
+{
+    static bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* env = getenv("WEBKIT_CHECKERBOARD_DURING_SCROLL");
+        return env && *env && strcmp(env, "0");
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
